680
00:21:41,927 --> 00:21:43,227
Now, the playbook.

681
00:21:43,577 --> 00:21:44,402
Angle three.

682
00:21:44,582 --> 00:21:46,603
Ten moves to make your bank work

683
00:21:46,603 --> 00:21:48,750
for you, not the other way around.

684
00:21:49,099 --> 00:21:49,831
Move one.

685
00:21:50,011 --> 00:21:51,973
Move your savings to a high yield

686
00:21:51,973 --> 00:21:52,449
account.

687
00:21:52,629 --> 00:21:55,161
Keep checking wherever is convenient,

688
00:21:55,161 --> 00:21:57,829
but put your emergency fund and savings

689
00:21:57,829 --> 00:22:00,908
goals somewhere that pays a competitive rate,

690
00:22:00,908 --> 00:22:03,030
and make sure it's FDIC or NCUA

691
00:22:03,030 --> 00:22:03,577
insured.

692
00:22:03,757 --> 00:22:06,489
This single move often earns people hundreds

693
00:22:06,489 --> 00:22:08,787
of dollars a year for fifteen minutes

694
00:22:08,787 --> 00:22:09,283
of work.

695
00:22:09,633 --> 00:22:10,376
Move two.

696
00:22:10,556 --> 00:22:13,398
Turn off overdraft coverage for debit card

697
00:22:13,398 --> 00:22:15,495
purchases if you don't need it,

698
00:22:15,495 --> 00:22:17,525
or link a savings account as a

699
00:22:17,525 --> 00:22:17,998
backup.

700
00:22:18,178 --> 00:22:19,142
Move three.

701
00:22:19,322 --> 00:22:21,110
Avoid monthly fees.

702
00:22:21,290 --> 00:22:22,650
Meet the conditions,

703
00:22:22,650 --> 00:22:24,079
ask for a fee waiver,

704
00:22:24,079 --> 00:22:26,120
or switch to a no fee account.

705
00:22:26,300 --> 00:22:29,120
Many online banks and credit unions charge

706
00:22:29,120 --> 00:22:30,665
no monthly fees at all.

707
00:22:31,015 --> 00:22:31,840
Move four.

708
00:22:32,020 --> 00:22:33,497
Use in network ATMs,

709
00:22:33,497 --> 00:22:36,155
or choose a bank that reimburses ATM

710
00:22:36,155 --> 00:22:36,524
fees.

711
00:22:36,704 --> 00:22:37,680
Move five.

712
00:22:37,860 --> 00:22:39,113
Set up alerts.

713
00:22:39,293 --> 00:22:40,820
Low balance alerts,

714
00:22:40,820 --> 00:22:44,355
large transaction alerts and deposit alerts.

715
00:22:44,535 --> 00:22:47,351
They're free, and they prevent most overdrafts

716
00:22:47,351 --> 00:22:48,819
and catch fraud quickly.

717
00:22:49,169 --> 00:22:50,446
Move six.

718
00:22:50,626 --> 00:22:51,764
Shop every loan.

719
00:22:51,944 --> 00:22:53,187
Before a mortgage,

720
00:22:53,187 --> 00:22:54,981
car loan or personal loan,

721
00:22:54,981 --> 00:22:57,672
get quotes from at least three lenders,

722
00:22:57,672 --> 00:22:59,398
including a credit union.

723
00:22:59,578 --> 00:23:00,664
Compare the APR,

724
00:23:00,664 --> 00:23:02,631
not just the monthly payment.

725
00:23:02,811 --> 00:23:03,641
On big loans,

726
00:23:03,641 --> 00:23:06,323
a small rate difference can mean thousands

727
00:23:06,323 --> 00:23:07,026
of dollars.

728
00:23:07,375 --> 00:23:08,362
Move seven.

729
00:23:08,542 --> 00:23:10,887
Say no to products you don't understand.

730
00:23:11,067 --> 00:23:13,696
If the person recommending a product can't

731
00:23:13,696 --> 00:23:15,323
explain its costs clearly,

732
00:23:15,323 --> 00:23:16,513
that's your answer.

733
00:23:16,693 --> 00:23:17,412
Move eight.

734
00:23:17,592 --> 00:23:19,624
Keep your investments low cost.

735
00:23:19,804 --> 00:23:22,789
Compare any bank investment product with low

736
00:23:22,789 --> 00:23:24,959
cost index funds at a brokerage,

737
00:23:24,959 --> 00:23:27,130
and look at the fees in dollars.

738
00:23:27,480 --> 00:23:28,270
Move nine.

739
00:23:28,450 --> 00:23:30,122
Review your bank once a year.

740
00:23:30,302 --> 00:23:31,648
Same day every year,

741
00:23:31,648 --> 00:23:32,793
check your rates,

742
00:23:32,793 --> 00:23:34,005
fees and accounts.

743
00:23:34,185 --> 00:23:36,484
Ask your bank to match competitors.

744
00:23:36,664 --> 00:23:37,939
If they won't,

745
00:23:37,939 --> 00:23:38,394
move.

746
00:23:38,574 --> 00:23:39,816
And move ten.

747
00:23:39,996 --> 00:23:42,154
Use the bank's business model in your

748
00:23:42,154 --> 00:23:42,504
favor.

749
00:23:42,684 --> 00:23:45,042
Take advantage of sign up bonuses when

750
00:23:45,042 --> 00:23:46,034
they make sense,

751
00:23:46,034 --> 00:23:47,586
pay credit cards in full,

752
00:23:47,586 --> 00:23:49,695
and keep your money where it earns

753
00:23:49,695 --> 00:23:50,254
the most.

754
00:23:50,603 --> 00:23:52,930
Moving twenty thousand dollars from a low

755
00:23:52,930 --> 00:23:55,143
rate account to a four percent account,

756
00:23:55,143 --> 00:23:57,355
and adding two hundred dollars a month,

757
00:23:57,355 --> 00:23:58,150
for ten years.

758
00:23:58,330 --> 00:23:59,978
Here's roughly where it could grow.

759
00:24:00,328 --> 00:24:01,663
That's an illustration,

760
00:24:01,663 --> 00:24:03,869
with rates that will change over time.

761
00:24:04,049 --> 00:24:06,549
But notice that this growth comes with

762
00:24:06,549 --> 00:24:08,392
no stock market risk at all,

763
00:24:08,392 --> 00:24:10,563
just a better rate on safe money.

764
00:24:10,743 --> 00:24:12,960
Banks count on most people never making

765
00:24:12,960 --> 00:24:13,529
this move.

766
00:24:13,709 --> 00:24:14,951
You can be the exception.

767
00:24:15,301 --> 00:24:16,962
Let's compare two savers.

768
00:24:17,142 --> 00:24:19,961
Patricia has thirty thousand dollars in savings

769
00:24:19,961 --> 00:24:21,760
at the big bank she's used for

770
00:24:21,760 --> 00:24:22,540
twenty years.

771
00:24:22,720 --> 00:24:24,759
The rate is a fraction of one

772
00:24:24,759 --> 00:24:25,321
percent.

773
00:24:25,501 --> 00:24:27,752
She pays a twelve dollar monthly fee

774
00:24:27,752 --> 00:24:30,567
on her checking because her balance sometimes

775
00:24:30,567 --> 00:24:32,005
dips below the minimum,

776
00:24:32,005 --> 00:24:34,570
and she's been charged two overdraft fees

777
00:24:34,570 --> 00:24:35,195
this year.

778
00:24:35,545 --> 00:24:36,175
In a year,

779
00:24:36,175 --> 00:24:38,883
Patricia earns maybe one hundred dollars in

780
00:24:38,883 --> 00:24:41,527
interest and pays about two hundred twenty

781
00:24:41,527 --> 00:24:42,535
dollars in fees.

782
00:24:42,715 --> 00:24:44,955
Her bank relationship costs her money.

783
00:24:45,135 --> 00:24:46,307
She doesn't notice,

784
00:24:46,307 --> 00:24:48,405
because the fees are small and the

785
00:24:48,405 --> 00:24:50,255
missing interest is invisible.

786
00:24:50,605 --> 00:24:52,451
Kevin has the same thirty thousand.

787
00:24:52,631 --> 00:24:54,804
His checking account is at a credit

788
00:24:54,804 --> 00:24:56,418
union with no monthly fee,

789
00:24:56,418 --> 00:24:58,281
and his savings are in an FDIC

790
00:24:58,281 --> 00:25:01,074
insured high yield account paying around four

791
00:25:01,074 --> 00:25:01,571
percent.

792
00:25:01,751 --> 00:25:04,585
He turned off overdraft coverage and set

793
00:25:04,585 --> 00:25:05,931
low balance alerts.

794
00:25:06,111 --> 00:25:08,166
He spent one afternoon setting it up.

795
00:25:08,515 --> 00:25:09,140
In a year,

796
00:25:09,140 --> 00:25:11,952
Kevin earns roughly twelve hundred dollars in

797
00:25:11,952 --> 00:25:14,077
interest and pays nothing in fees.

798
00:25:14,257 --> 00:25:16,694
The gap between Patricia and Kevin is

799
00:25:16,694 --> 00:25:19,460
more than thirteen hundred dollars a year,

800
00:25:19,460 --> 00:25:21,897
with exactly the same amount of money

801
00:25:21,897 --> 00:25:24,334
and exactly the same level of safety.

802
00:25:24,514 --> 00:25:25,410
Over ten years,

803
00:25:25,410 --> 00:25:27,977
that's well over thirteen thousand dollars,

804
00:25:27,977 --> 00:25:30,783
before counting any interest on the difference.

805
00:25:31,133 --> 00:25:33,084
Same thirty thousand dollars.

806
00:25:33,264 --> 00:25:34,332
Same safety.

807
00:25:34,512 --> 00:25:36,846
Very different results in a single year.

808
00:25:37,195 --> 00:25:37,956
To be fair,

809
00:25:37,956 --> 00:25:40,445
let's talk about what banks do well,

810
00:25:40,445 --> 00:25:43,349
because this isn't a story about villains.

811
00:25:43,529 --> 00:25:45,947
Banks make it possible to get paid

812
00:25:45,947 --> 00:25:48,579
electronically, pay bills in seconds,

813
00:25:48,579 --> 00:25:50,998
and keep money safe from theft and

814
00:25:50,998 --> 00:25:51,354
fire.

815
00:25:51,534 --> 00:25:54,198
They fund mortgages that let families own

816
00:25:54,198 --> 00:25:56,928
homes, and loans that help businesses grow

817
00:25:56,928 --> 00:25:57,513
and hire.

818
00:25:57,693 --> 00:26:00,782
Without banks, modern economic life would barely

819
00:26:00,782 --> 00:26:01,362
function.

820
00:26:01,711 --> 00:26:04,962
Banks also carry real risks and costs.

821
00:26:05,142 --> 00:26:06,570
Some loans aren't repaid.

822
00:26:06,750 --> 00:26:09,003
Fraud costs them billions.

823
00:26:09,183 --> 00:26:12,043
Regulation requires them to hold capital,

824
00:26:12,043 --> 00:26:15,393
follow strict rules and run expensive compliance

825
00:26:15,393 --> 00:26:16,021
programs.

826
00:26:16,201 --> 00:26:19,730
Branches, staff and technology all cost money.

827
00:26:19,910 --> 00:26:22,106
Profit is how they cover those costs

828
00:26:22,106 --> 00:26:23,753
and pay their shareholders.

829
00:26:24,103 --> 00:26:25,795
So the goal isn't to hate your

830
00:26:25,795 --> 00:26:26,077
bank.

831
00:26:26,257 --> 00:26:28,300
It's to be an informed customer.

832
00:26:28,480 --> 00:26:30,673
Use the services that give you real

833
00:26:30,673 --> 00:26:33,116
value, avoid the products and fees that

834
00:26:33,116 --> 00:26:35,308
don't, and make sure your own money

835
00:26:35,308 --> 00:26:36,561
earns a fair return.

836
00:26:36,741 --> 00:26:39,423
Banks respond to customers who shop around.

837
00:26:39,603 --> 00:26:41,449
That's how competition works.

838
00:26:41,798 --> 00:26:42,770
In recent years,

839
00:26:42,770 --> 00:26:45,382
many financial apps have appeared that look

840
00:26:45,382 --> 00:26:46,779
like banks, but aren't.

841
00:26:46,959 --> 00:26:49,775
Some are technology companies that partner with

842
00:26:49,775 --> 00:26:51,812
a licensed bank behind the scenes.

843
00:26:51,992 --> 00:26:54,016
They can offer great features,

844
00:26:54,016 --> 00:26:55,298
like early paydays,

845
00:26:55,298 --> 00:26:58,064
budgeting tools and higher savings rates.

846
00:26:58,244 --> 00:27:00,387
But it's important to know who actually

847
00:27:00,387 --> 00:27:01,321
holds your money.

848
00:27:01,670 --> 00:27:03,123
In twenty twenty four,

849
00:27:03,123 --> 00:27:04,774
a company called Synapse,

850
00:27:04,774 --> 00:27:07,877
which connected several popular apps to partner

851
00:27:07,877 --> 00:27:09,263
banks, went bankrupt.

852
00:27:09,443 --> 00:27:12,060
Many customers of those apps found their

853
00:27:12,060 --> 00:27:13,631
money frozen for months,

854
00:27:13,631 --> 00:27:15,724
and some reported missing funds.

855
00:27:15,904 --> 00:27:17,913
The lesson isn't to avoid apps.

856
00:27:18,093 --> 00:27:19,753
It's to read the fine print.

857
00:27:19,933 --> 00:27:22,224
Check which bank holds your deposits,

858
00:27:22,224 --> 00:27:23,834
whether it's FDIC insured,

859
00:27:23,834 --> 00:27:26,001
and whether your balance is held in

860
00:27:26,001 --> 00:27:26,620
your name.

861
00:27:26,970 --> 00:27:28,752
Here's a short script you can use

862
00:27:28,752 --> 00:27:30,047
when you call your bank.

863
00:27:30,227 --> 00:27:32,456
It works more often than people think.

864
00:27:32,806 --> 00:27:33,817
Start friendly.

865
00:27:33,997 --> 00:27:35,890
Hi, I've been a customer for a

866
00:27:35,890 --> 00:27:38,478
long time, and I'm reviewing my accounts.

867
00:27:38,658 --> 00:27:39,668
Then be specific.

868
00:27:39,848 --> 00:27:41,972
I've been charged a monthly fee and

869
00:27:41,972 --> 00:27:43,610
an overdraft fee this year.

870
00:27:43,790 --> 00:27:44,602
Could you waive them?

871
00:27:44,782 --> 00:27:46,971
Many banks have the power to refund

872
00:27:46,971 --> 00:27:49,534
fees, especially for long time customers,

873
00:27:49,534 --> 00:27:51,847
and they'd rather keep you happy than

874
00:27:51,847 --> 00:27:52,410
lose you.

875
00:27:52,760 --> 00:27:53,945
Then ask about rates.

876
00:27:54,125 --> 00:27:56,585
My savings account pays much less than

877
00:27:56,585 --> 00:27:57,944
insured online banks.

878
00:27:58,124 --> 00:27:59,953
Do you have a better savings option

879
00:27:59,953 --> 00:28:00,319
for me?

880
00:28:00,499 --> 00:28:01,868
If they offer something,

881
00:28:01,868 --> 00:28:02,496
compare it.

882
00:28:02,676 --> 00:28:03,602
If they don't,

883
00:28:03,602 --> 00:28:05,787
thank them and move your savings.

884
00:28:05,967 --> 00:28:06,793
And on loans,

885
00:28:06,793 --> 00:28:09,018
ask whether you qualify for a lower

886
00:28:09,018 --> 00:28:11,052
rate given your payment history.

887
00:28:11,402 --> 00:28:13,203
Stay polite, keep it short,

888
00:28:13,203 --> 00:28:15,071
and don't be afraid of a no.

889
00:28:15,251 --> 00:28:17,629
The worst outcome is that nothing changes,

890
00:28:17,629 --> 00:28:19,384
and you move your money anyway.

891
00:28:19,564 --> 00:28:21,364
The best outcome is that a ten

892
00:28:21,364 --> 00:28:23,823
minute call saves you hundreds of dollars

893
00:28:23,823 --> 00:28:24,243
a year.

894
00:28:24,593 --> 00:28:25,917
Before the questions,

895
00:28:25,917 --> 00:28:28,248
five red flags that your bank account

896
00:28:28,248 --> 00:28:29,760
is costing you too much.

897
00:28:29,940 --> 00:28:30,160
One.

898
00:28:30,340 --> 00:28:32,535
Your savings rate is a tiny fraction

899
00:28:32,535 --> 00:28:34,973
of what insured online banks are paying.

900
00:28:35,153 --> 00:28:35,524
Two.

901
00:28:35,704 --> 00:28:37,787
You've paid a monthly maintenance fee in

902
00:28:37,787 --> 00:28:38,932
the last three months.

903
00:28:39,112 --> 00:28:39,542
Three.

904
00:28:39,722 --> 00:28:42,588
You've paid an overdraft or insufficient funds

905
00:28:42,588 --> 00:28:43,460
fee this year.

906
00:28:43,809 --> 00:28:44,367
Four.

907
00:28:44,547 --> 00:28:47,126
You regularly pay out of network ATM

908
00:28:47,126 --> 00:28:47,484
fees.

909
00:28:47,664 --> 00:28:48,604
And five.

910
00:28:48,784 --> 00:28:51,500
You've bought an investment or insurance product

911
00:28:51,500 --> 00:28:54,102
from your bank without comparing it elsewhere.

912
00:28:54,282 --> 00:28:55,932
If you see two or more of

913
00:28:55,932 --> 00:28:58,439
these, block out one afternoon and run

914
00:28:58,439 --> 00:28:59,297
the playbook.

915
00:28:59,477 --> 00:29:01,833
It's one of the highest paying afternoons

916
00:29:01,833 --> 00:29:02,867
you'll ever spend.

917
00:29:03,217 --> 00:29:05,530
Let me answer the questions people ask

918
00:29:05,530 --> 00:29:06,747
me most about banks.

919
00:29:07,096 --> 00:29:07,874
Question one.

920
00:29:08,054 --> 00:29:09,308
Are online banks safe?

921
00:29:09,488 --> 00:29:11,204
If they're FDIC insured,

922
00:29:11,204 --> 00:29:14,065
deposits are protected up to the limits,

923
00:29:14,065 --> 00:29:15,781
just like at a big bank.

924
00:29:15,961 --> 00:29:18,596
Check the FDIC's official BankFind tool.

925
00:29:18,776 --> 00:29:21,049
Some apps are not banks themselves but

926
00:29:21,049 --> 00:29:22,186
partner with banks,

927
00:29:22,186 --> 00:29:24,458
so make sure you understand which bank

928
00:29:24,458 --> 00:29:26,970
actually holds your money and whether it's

929
00:29:26,970 --> 00:29:27,449
insured.

930
00:29:27,798 --> 00:29:28,623
Question two.

931
00:29:28,803 --> 00:29:30,472
Is a credit union better than a

932
00:29:30,472 --> 00:29:30,742
bank?

933
00:29:30,922 --> 00:29:33,579
Credit unions are member owned nonprofits,

934
00:29:33,579 --> 00:29:35,794
and they often offer lower fees and

935
00:29:35,794 --> 00:29:36,933
better loan rates,

936
00:29:36,933 --> 00:29:38,515
especially on auto loans.

937
00:29:38,695 --> 00:29:41,632
Banks may offer more branches and technology.

938
00:29:41,812 --> 00:29:43,507
Many people use both.

939
00:29:43,687 --> 00:29:46,524
A credit union for loans and checking,

940
00:29:46,524 --> 00:29:48,988
and an online bank for high yield

941
00:29:48,988 --> 00:29:49,585
savings.

942
00:29:49,934 --> 00:29:51,037
Question three.

943
00:29:51,217 --> 00:29:53,179
Should I keep money in a CD?

944
00:29:53,359 --> 00:29:55,994
A certificate of deposit locks your money

945
00:29:55,994 --> 00:29:57,601
for a set time at a fixed

946
00:29:57,601 --> 00:29:57,922
rate.

947
00:29:58,102 --> 00:30:00,118
It can make sense for money you

948
00:30:00,118 --> 00:30:02,263
won't need until a specific date,

949
00:30:02,263 --> 00:30:04,929
especially if rates are expected to fall.

950
00:30:05,109 --> 00:30:07,569
But early withdrawals usually come with a

951
00:30:07,569 --> 00:30:10,029
penalty, so don't put your emergency fund

952
00:30:10,029 --> 00:30:10,449
in one.

953
00:30:10,799 --> 00:30:11,659
Question four.

954
00:30:11,839 --> 00:30:14,079
How do I switch banks without chaos?

955
00:30:14,259 --> 00:30:15,734
Open the new account first.

956
00:30:15,914 --> 00:30:17,411
Move your direct deposit.

957
00:30:17,591 --> 00:30:20,178
Then move automatic payments one by one

958
00:30:20,178 --> 00:30:21,504
over a month or two.

959
00:30:21,684 --> 00:30:23,302
Keep the old account open,

960
00:30:23,302 --> 00:30:24,609
with a small balance,

961
00:30:24,609 --> 00:30:27,036
until you're sure everything has moved.

962
00:30:27,216 --> 00:30:28,099
Then close it.

963
00:30:28,279 --> 00:30:29,342
It's a project,

964
00:30:29,342 --> 00:30:30,264
not a crisis.

965
00:30:30,613 --> 00:30:31,658
Question five.

966
00:30:31,838 --> 00:30:33,603
Do banks really lend out my money?

967
00:30:33,783 --> 00:30:34,271
Yes.

968
00:30:34,451 --> 00:30:35,681
That's the business.

969
00:30:35,861 --> 00:30:38,276
Banks hold some cash and reserves,

970
00:30:38,276 --> 00:30:40,406
and lend or invest much of the

971
00:30:40,406 --> 00:30:40,761
rest.

972
00:30:40,941 --> 00:30:44,045
This system is why deposit insurance and

973
00:30:44,045 --> 00:30:47,459
regulation exist, to protect depositors if a

974
00:30:47,459 --> 00:30:48,313
bank fails.

975
00:30:48,663 --> 00:30:49,674
Question seven.

976
00:30:49,854 --> 00:30:51,990
Is it worth chasing bank sign up

977
00:30:51,990 --> 00:30:52,524
bonuses?

978
00:30:52,704 --> 00:30:53,609
Sometimes.

979
00:30:53,789 --> 00:30:56,022
Some banks pay a few hundred dollars

980
00:30:56,022 --> 00:30:58,316
for opening an account and setting up

981
00:30:58,316 --> 00:30:59,246
direct deposit.

982
00:30:59,426 --> 00:31:01,504
If the requirements are easy and there

983
00:31:01,504 --> 00:31:02,160
are no fees,

984
00:31:02,160 --> 00:31:03,199
it can be worth it.

985
00:31:03,379 --> 00:31:05,325
But read the conditions carefully,

986
00:31:05,325 --> 00:31:07,385
and don't open so many accounts that

987
00:31:07,385 --> 00:31:08,244
you lose track.

988
00:31:08,594 --> 00:31:10,172
And question six.

989
00:31:10,352 --> 00:31:11,878
What's the one thing I should do

990
00:31:11,878 --> 00:31:12,164
today?

991
00:31:12,344 --> 00:31:14,072
Look up the interest rate on your

992
00:31:14,072 --> 00:31:14,909
savings account.

993
00:31:15,089 --> 00:31:16,594
Then look up the rate on a

994
00:31:16,594 --> 00:31:18,735
few FDIC insured high yield accounts.

995
00:31:18,915 --> 00:31:20,451
If the difference is large,

996
00:31:20,451 --> 00:31:22,669
you've just found free money waiting to

997
00:31:22,669 --> 00:31:23,408
be collected.

998
00:31:23,758 --> 00:31:24,582
Quick recap.

999
00:31:24,762 --> 00:31:27,224
Banks make money from the spread,

1000
00:31:27,224 --> 00:31:30,058
paying you little and lending at more,

1001
00:31:30,058 --> 00:31:31,849
from all kinds of loans,

1002
00:31:31,849 --> 00:31:33,340
from overdraft fees,

1003
00:31:33,340 --> 00:31:35,578
from monthly and service fees,

1004
00:31:35,578 --> 00:31:37,294
from debit card swipes,

1005
00:31:37,294 --> 00:31:39,607
from selling you more products,

1006
00:31:39,607 --> 00:31:40,726
and from float.

1007
00:31:41,076 --> 00:31:42,877
We stay because of inertia,

1008
00:31:42,877 --> 00:31:44,145
the appeal of free,

1009
00:31:44,145 --> 00:31:46,079
the feeling that big is safe,

1010
00:31:46,079 --> 00:31:49,415
convenience, complexity, and the invisible cost of

1011
00:31:49,415 --> 00:31:51,083
interest we never earned.

1012
00:31:51,434 --> 00:31:52,819
And the playbook:

1013
00:31:52,819 --> 00:31:54,369
high yield savings,

1014
00:31:54,369 --> 00:31:57,304
overdraft settings, no monthly fees,

1015
00:31:57,304 --> 00:31:58,608
in network ATMs,

1016
00:31:58,608 --> 00:32:00,565
alerts, shop every loan,

1017
00:32:00,565 --> 00:32:03,418
skip products you don't understand,

1018
00:32:03,418 --> 00:32:05,538
keep investments low cost,

1019
00:32:05,538 --> 00:32:07,087
review once a year,

1020
00:32:07,087 --> 00:32:09,777
and use the system in your favor.

1021
00:32:10,128 --> 00:32:11,657
If you want the full plan for

1022
00:32:11,657 --> 00:32:13,345
making every dollar work harder,

1023
00:32:13,345 --> 00:32:14,400
it's in my playbook.

1024
00:32:14,580 --> 00:32:16,356
The link is in the description.

1025
00:32:16,536 --> 00:32:18,316
And watch my video on how credit

1026
00:32:18,316 --> 00:32:20,263
card companies make money from you.

1027
00:32:20,443 --> 00:32:22,242
It's the other half of the banking

1028
00:32:22,242 --> 00:32:22,719
business.

1029
00:32:22,899 --> 00:32:24,129
I'm Ryan Rover.

1030
00:32:24,309 --> 00:32:25,436
See you in the next one.
